      "content": "Directly hooking a legacy DB to a modern cloud API without an integration layer is highly risky and likely to cause major issues. There are probably significant differences in data formats, communication protocols, and security models between the two systems. Bypassing the integration phase increases the risk of data corruption, instability, and unforeseen bugs that will almost certainly extend your timeline beyond two weeks. I strongly advise maintaining a rigorous integration plan to ensure a stable and reliable migration.",
